        "original_id": "8d552a56-1dc8-5f71-b4ec-c849940f6468",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Simon Helberg, Jeremy Konner, Jason Ritter, Jocelyn Towne\n- Music: Army Navy, The Last Place, Ode to Janice Melt, The Fever Zone\n- Film and TV: The Big Bang Theory, We'll Never Have Paris, Howard Wolowitz\n- Awards: Critics' Choice Television Award\n\nFacts:\n- Simon Helberg was born on December 9, 1980, and he is an American actor, comedian, and musician.\n- Simon Helberg is best known for playing Howard Wolowitz in the sitcom The Big Bang Theory, which began in 2007.\n- The Last Place is the second studio album by the American indie rock band Army Navy, and it was released on July 12, 2011, on the band's own label The Fever Zone.\n- A music video for Army Navy's song Ode to Janice Melt was released on September 15, 2011, and it was directed by Jeremy Konner and starred Jason Ritter and Simon Helberg.\n- Simon Helberg won a Critics' Choice Television Award in 2013 for his work on The Big Bang Theory.\n- We'll Never Have Paris is a 2014 American romantic comedy directed by Simon Helberg in his directorial debut and by Jocelyn Towne.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
